{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordPositionTracking","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordPositionTracking","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordComponentStructure"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordPositionTracking.allEven_posAfter_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordPositionTracking.allEven_posAfter_self","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MonotoneWordPositionTracking.lean#L144-L151","doc":"…and with all exponents even (`e ≡ 2`) no run swaps, so position `g` still holds\nstrand `g` — the maximally-split case, matching `allEven_compIdx`'s singleton\ncomponents. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordPositionTracking.allOdd_posAfter_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordPositionTracking.allOdd_posAfter_self","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MonotoneWordPositionTracking.lean#L134-L142","doc":"**Not vacuous, and it exercises both branches.** With all exponents odd (`e ≡ 1`)\nevery run swaps, so the left strand is carried the whole way and stays `0`; the sibling\n`allOdd_compIdx` says all strands are then in one component, so this is the\nmaximally-fused case. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordPositionTracking.crossing_pair_of_run","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordPositionTracking.crossing_pair_of_run","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MonotoneWordPositionTracking.lean#L126-L132","doc":"**The two together: run `g` crosses exactly the strands `(pStart e g, g+1)`.**\n\nTier 1 of `eps_eq` was resting on this sentence; it is now a theorem about the position\nrecursion rather than a reading of the probe. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordPositionTracking.posAfter_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordPositionTracking.posAfter_self","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MonotoneWordPositionTracking.lean#L113-L124","doc":"**`pStart` is the correct recursion.** Position `g` holds `pStart e g` when run `R_g`\nbegins — an even run restores the pair so the next run's left strand is `g+1`, an odd\nrun swaps them so the left strand is carried over unchanged.\n\nThis is what `MonotoneWordComponentStructure` assumed about its own definition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordPositionTracking.posAfter_succ_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordPositionTracking.posAfter_succ_self","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MonotoneWordPositionTracking.lean#L107-L111","doc":"**Position `g+1` still holds strand `g+1` when run `R_g` begins.** The observation\nthe entire tier-1 argument rests on: the pair that run `g` will cross is fixed before it\nstarts, so all `e_g` of its crossings are between the same two strands. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordPositionTracking.posAfter_of_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordPositionTracking.posAfter_of_le","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MonotoneWordPositionTracking.lean#L96-L105","doc":"**The invariant, and it is where ascending order is used.** After `g` runs, every\nposition at or beyond `g+1` still holds its original strand: run `h < g` moves only\npositions `h` and `h+1`, both `≤ g`, so it cannot reach that far. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordPositionTracking.posAfter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordPositionTracking.posAfter","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MonotoneWordPositionTracking.lean#L87-L94","doc":"The position→strand map after runs `0, …, g-1` have executed.\n\n`e_g` crossings of one adjacent pair compose to the identity when `e_g` is even and to a\nsingle swap when it is odd, so only the parity of the exponent survives — which is why\nthis is a one-step recursion rather than an iteration. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordPositionTracking.swapAt_of_gt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordPositionTracking.swapAt_of_gt","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MonotoneWordPositionTracking.lean#L82-L85","doc":"A position beyond the pair is fixed by the swap. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordPositionTracking.swapAt_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordPositionTracking.swapAt_right","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MonotoneWordPositionTracking.lean#L79-L80","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordPositionTracking.swapAt_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordPositionTracking.swapAt_left","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MonotoneWordPositionTracking.lean#L77-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordPositionTracking.swapAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordPositionTracking.swapAt","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MonotoneWordPositionTracking.lean#L74-L75","doc":"Transposition of positions `g` and `g+1`, as a function on position indices. ","signatureChunk":0}]}